/-!
Proof of the conjectured order-3 recurrence for A386834.

1. With `j = n - k` and `n = m + 1`, `a(m+1) = Σ_j F(m, j)`, `F(m, j) = C(4m+5, 3m+4+j) C(3m+2+j, j)`
   (symmetry of the binomial coefficient; no truncated subtraction remains, and `F(m, j) = 0` for
   `j ≥ m + 2`).
2. Zeilberger's algorithm gives `K(m) (c₀ F(m, j) + c₁ F(m+1, j) + c₂ F(m+2, j)) = H(m, j+1) - H(m, j)`
   with polynomial `cᵢ`, `K` and `H(m, j) = h(m, j) C(4m+12, 3m+9+j) C(3m+2+j, j)`. It is checked for all
   `m, j` by `linear_combination`, after relating every binomial to `C(4m+12, 3m+9+j)` and
   `C(3m+2+j, j)` through Pascal-type ratio identities (`diag_z`, `vert_z`, `jup_z`).
3. Summing over `j < m + 4` (`H` vanishes at both ends) gives the order-2 recurrence `Z`.
4. The conjectured order-3 operator is `(p S + q)` times the order-2 one: with
   `d(m) = 77m^3 + 577m^2 + 1436m + 1188 > 0`, `d(m) · conj(m+4) = -6(39221117m + 105934708) Z(m)
   - (16543753m + 39179079) Z(m+1)`. The case `n = 3` is checked directly.
-/

